"விசை","parts":[{"text":"விசை","lemma":"vicai","gloss":"speed"}],"gloss":"speed"},{"surface":"கத","parts":[{"text":"கத","lemma":"kata","gloss":"angry"}],"gloss":"angry"},{"surface":"நாய்","parts":[{"text":"நாய்","lemma":"nāy","gloss":"dog"}],"gloss":"dog"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நோன்","parts":[{"text":"நோன்","lemma":"nōṉ","gloss":"strong"}],"gloss":"strong"},{"surface":"சிலை","parts":[{"text":"சிலை","lemma":"cilai","gloss":"bow"}],"gloss":"bow"},{"surface":"வேட்டுவ","parts":[{"text":"வேட்டுவ","lemma":"vēṭṭuva","gloss":"hunter (vocative)"}],"gloss":"O hunter!"},{"surface":"நோய்","parts":[{"text":"நோய்","lemma":"nōy","gloss":"suffering"}],"gloss":"suffering"},{"surface":"இலை","parts":[{"text":"இலை","lemma":"ilai","gloss":"without"}],"gloss":"without"},{"surface":"ஆகுக","parts":[{"text":"ஆகுக","lemma":"ākuka","gloss":"may you be"}],"gloss":"may you be"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஆர்கலி","parts":[{"text":"ஆர்கலி","lemma":"ārkali","gloss":"roaring ocean"}],"gloss":"roaring ocean"},{"surface":"யாணர்","parts":[{"text":"யாணர்","lemma":"yāṇar","gloss":"prosperity"}],"gloss":"prosperity"},{"surface":"தரீஇய","parts":[{"text":"தரீஇய","lemma":"tarīiya","gloss":"to bring"}],"gloss":"to bring"},{"surface":"கால்","parts":[{"text":"கால்","lemma":"kāl","gloss":"cloud columns"}],"gloss":"cloud columns"},{"surface":"வீழ்த்து","parts":[{"text":"வீழ்த்து","lemma":"vīḻttu","gloss":"letting down"}],"gloss":"letting down"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கடல்","parts":[{"text":"கடல்","lemma":"kaṭal","gloss":"ocean"}],"gloss":"ocean"},{"surface":"வயின்","parts":[{"text":"வயின்","lemma":"vayiṉ","gloss":"in"}],"gloss":"in"},{"surface":"குழீஇய","parts":[{"text":"குழீஇய","lemma":"kuḻīiya","gloss":"gathered"}],"gloss":"gathered"},{"surface":"அண்ணல்","parts":[{"text":"அண்ணல்","lemma":"aṇṇal","gloss":"majestic"}],"gloss":"majestic"},{"surface":"அம்","parts":[{"text":"அம்","lemma":"am","gloss":"beautiful"}],"gloss":"beautiful"},{"surface":"கொண்மூ","parts":[{"text":"கொண்மூ","lemma":"koṇmū","gloss":"cloud"}],"gloss":"cloud"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நீர்","parts":[{"text":"நீர்","lemma":"nīr","gloss":"water"}],"gloss":"water"},{"surface":"இன்று","parts":[{"text":"இன்று","lemma":"iṉṟu","gloss":"without"}],"gloss":"without"},{"surface":"பெயரா","parts":[{"text":"பெயரா","lemma":"peyarā","gloss":"not returning"}],"gloss":"not returning"},{"surface":"ஆங்கு","parts":[{"text":"ஆங்கு","lemma":"āṅku","gloss":"like that"}],"gloss":"like that"},{"surface":"தேரொடு","parts":[{"text":"தேரொடு","lemma":"tēroṭu","gloss":"with chariot"}],"gloss":"with chariot"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஒளிறு","parts":[{"text":"ஒளிறு","lemma":"oḷiṟu","gloss":"shining"}],"gloss":"shining"},{"surface":"மறுப்பு","parts":[{"text":"மறுப்பு","lemma":"maṟuppu","gloss":"tusk"}],"gloss":"tusk"},{"surface":"ஏந்திய","parts":[{"text":"ஏந்திய","lemma":"ēntiya","gloss":"holding high"}],"gloss":"holding high"},{"surface":"செம்மல்","parts":[{"text":"செம்மல்","lemma":"cemmal","gloss":"majestic"}],"gloss":"majestic"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"களிறு","parts":[{"text":"களிறு","lemma":"kaḷiṟu","gloss":"male elephant"}],"gloss":"male elephant"},{"surface":"இன்று","parts":[{"text":"இன்று","lemma":"iṉṟu","gloss":"without"}],"gloss":"without"},{"surface":"பெயரல","parts":[{"text":"பெயரல","lemma":"peyarala","gloss":"will not return"}],"gloss":"will not return"},{"surface":"பரிசிலர்","parts":[{"text":"பரிசிலர்","lemma":"paricilar","gloss":"seekers of gifts"}],"gloss":"seekers of gifts"},{"surface":"கடும்பே","parts":[{"text":"கடும்பு","lemma":"kaṭumpu","gloss":"kinsmen"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"kinsmen"}]}],"literal":"Even if they are the three kings of complete wealth, / giving without love, we do not desire indeed. / With victorious anger abated, fast galloping horses, / becoming a refuge for those who approach, and destroying enemies' / effort and heart, with sword-abundant army, / O warrior of Kōṭai hill fenced with white flowers! / Blocking both small and big paths, / destroying herds of deer, with swift speed and angry dogs, / O hunter with a strong bow! May you be free of suffering! / To bring prosperity to the roaring ocean, letting down cloud-legs, / gathered in the ocean, the majestic beautiful cloud / does not return without water; like that, with chariot / and shining tusk-bearing majestic / male elephant, without them, the kinsmen of seekers of gifts will not return.","translation":"Even if they are the three great kings of complete wealth, we do not desire their gifts if given without love. O warrior of Kōṭai hill fenced with white flowers, who has fast-galloping horses whose victorious fury has calmed, who is a refuge for those who seek you, and whose sword-wielding army destroys the strength and resolve of enemies! O hunter with a strong bow, who hunts with angry, swift dogs that block all paths, small and large, to destroy herds of deer! May you be free of suffering! Just like the majestic, beautiful cloud that gathers over the roaring ocean, letting down its rain-legs to bring prosperity, never returns without water, the kinsmen of bards who seek gifts will never return from you without a chariot and a majestic male elephant with shining tusks.","modern":"முழுமையான செல்வத்தைக் கொண்ட மூவேந்தர்களாகவே இருந்தாலும், அன்பு இல்லாமல் கொடுக்கும் கொடையை நாங்கள் விரும்ப மாட்டோம். வெண்மையான பூக்களை வேலியாகக் கொண்ட கோடை மலையின் தலைவனே! வெற்றி ஆவேசம் தணிந்த, வேகமாக ஓடும் குதிரைகளையும், உன்னிடம் அடைக்கலம் புகுவோருக்குப் புகலிடமாகவும் விளங்கி, பகைவர்களின் முயற்சியையும் மனவலிமையையும் அழிக்கும் வாள் ஏந்திய படையையும் உடையவனே! சிறிய வழிகளையும் பெரிய வழிகளையும் அடைத்து நின்று, மான்கூட்டங்களை அழிக்கும் வேகமும் சினமும் கொண்ட வேட்டை நாய்களையும், வலிமையான வில்லையும் உடைய வேட்டுவனே! நீ நோய் நொடியின்றி வாழ்வாயாக! முழங்குகின்ற கடலில் புகுந்து, உலகிற்குப் புதிய வளத்தைத் தருவதற்காகத் தன் மழைக்கால்களை இறக்கி, நீரைக் குடித்துத் திரண்ட அழகிய மேகம், நீரின்றித் திரும்பாது. அதுபோல, உன்னிடம் பரிசு பெற வந்த இரவலர்களின் சுற்றத்தார், தேருடனும் ஒளிரும் தந்தங்களை உடைய ஆண் யானையுடனும் அல்லாமல் வெறும் கையோடு உன்னிடமிருந்து திரும்ப மாட்டார்கள்.","explanation":"The poet Peruntalaiccāttaṉār is addressing the chieftain Kaṭiya Neṭuvēṭṭuvaṉ. He praises the chieftain's generosity and hunting skills, contrasting him with the three great kings of Tamil Nadu. The poet asserts that bards do not value gifts given without love, even if they come from the wealthiest rulers. In contrast, Neṭuvēṭṭuvaṉ gives with genuine affection and respect. The poem features a beautiful simile comparing the chieftain to a rain cloud. Just as a majestic cloud that gathers over the ocean never returns without water, the bards who visit Neṭuvēṭṭuvaṉ will never return to their families empty-handed, but always with grand gifts like chariots and elephants.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,0.9],[0.9,1.1],[1.1,1.5],[1.72,2.38],[2.68,2.99],[3.07,3.55],[3.55,3.8],[3.8,5.1],[5.1,5.5],[5.5,5.75],[5.75,5.88],[6.0,7.31],[7.31,7.64],[7.64,8.36],[8.41,8.7],[8.7,9.45],[9.45,9.45],[9.45,9.45],[9.45,9.82],[9.82,9.82],[9.82,10.2],[10.2,12.2],[12.2,12.5],[12.5,13.4],[13.4,13.5],[13.5,14.14],[14.4,14.8],[14.8,15.9],[15.9,16.1],[16.1,17.0],[17.0,17.3],[18.0,18.6],[18.6,18.8],[18.97,19.3],[19.3,19.8],[19.8,21.0],[21.0,21.2],[21.2,21.7],[21.7,22.1],[22.1,22.96],[22.96,23.06],[23.06,23.06],[23.06,23.06],[23.06,23.39],[23.6,25.6],[25.6,25.7],[25.7,26.0],[26.0,26.6],[26.6,28.2],[28.2,28.2],[28.2,29.3],[29.33,29.4],[29.4,30.1],[30.1,30.7],[30.7,30.8]],"female":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,0.9],[0.9,1.2],[1.2,1.6],[1.88,2.72],[3.08,3.39],[3.47,3.95],[3.95,4.01],[4.08,4.2],[4.88,6.0],[6.0,6.0],[6.0,6.0],[6.0,8.48],[8.48,8.48],[8.48,9.21],[9.21,10.15],[10.15,10.15],[10.15,10.15],[10.15,11.4],[11.4,11.8],[11.8,12.63],[12.8,13.3],[13.3,13.4],[13.4,13.7],[13.7,14.8],[14.8,15.0],[15.0,15.5],[15.9,16.4],[16.4,17.5],[17.5,17.6],[17.6,18.7],[18.7,19.2],[19.92,20.62],[20.62,20.82],[20.82,21.54],[21.54,22.02],[22.02,23.22],[23.22,23.42],[23.42,23.82],[23.82,24.22],[24.22,24.51],[24.51,24.54],[24.54,24.54],[24.5